    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="With only n replicates the standard deviation s is itself uncertain, so the interval \bar x\pm t\,s/\sqrt n from t_confidence_interval uses Student&#x27;s t instead of the normal 1.96. We simulate many triplicate analyses and show that the t interval covers the true value 95% of the time, while the naive \pm1.96\,s/\sqrt n interval falls well short.">

